# Bluenixx Build Guide

This document describes how to initialize the Bluenixx source tree, configure build options, and build a ROM.

## Prerequisites

Before building, prepare a Linux build environment and install the dependencies required by Android's build system. Refer to the [LineageOS build documentation](https://wiki.lineageos.org/) for environment setup and device-specific requirements.

Configure Git with the name and email you want associated with your commits:

```bash
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "you@example.com"
```

When prompted to authenticate for Android source access, follow the instructions shown by [Android Code Search / Gitiles](https://android.googlesource.com/).

## Initialize the source tree

Initialize the Bluenixx manifest on the `bluenixx-17.0` branch:

```bash
repo init -u https://github.com/Bluenixx/bluenixx-manifest.git -b bluenixx-17.0 --git-lfs
```

Synchronize the source repositories:

```bash
repo sync
```

Allow the initial sync to finish before starting the build. If synchronization fails, resolve the reported repository or network errors and run `repo sync` again.

## Build Bluenixx

From the root of the source tree, load the build environment and select a target. The following example uses the `bangkk` device:

```bash
source build/envsetup.sh
breakfast bangkk userdebug
mka bacon -j"$(nproc --all)"
```

Alternatively, select a product and build variant with a supported `lunch` target. Run `lunch` to see the available choices for your checkout.

The resulting ROM package is generated by the build system. The exact output depends on the selected device, build configuration, and build flags.

## Build configuration

Set these environment variables **before running `breakfast`** to configure the build:

| Variable | Supported values | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `RELEASE_TYPE` | `OFFICIAL`, `NIGHTLY`, `SNAPSHOT`, `EXPERIMENTAL` | Selects the release type. If unset or invalid, the build falls back to `UNOFFICIAL`. |
| `BLUENIXX_MAINTAINER` | Maintainer username | Required for an `OFFICIAL` build. The `maintainer:product` pair must be listed in `vendor/lineage/bluenixx.maintainers`; otherwise, the build falls back to `UNOFFICIAL`. |
| `WITH_GMS` | `true` or unset | When set to `true`, includes MindTheGapps from the `cinnamonbun` branch and marks the package as `GAPPS`. When unset, the package is marked `VANILLA`. |

### Example: Official build with GApps

```bash
export RELEASE_TYPE=OFFICIAL
export BLUENIXX_MAINTAINER=zedisspp
export WITH_GMS=true

breakfast bangkk
mka bacon -j"$(nproc --all)"
```

### Example: Unofficial vanilla build

```bash
unset RELEASE_TYPE BLUENIXX_MAINTAINER WITH_GMS

breakfast bangkk
mka bacon -j"$(nproc --all)"
```

### Package naming

The expected package naming format is:

```text
bluenixx-17.0-<DATE>-<TYPE>-<GAPPS|VANILLA>-<device>.zip
```

The final filename depends on the naming logic implemented by the source tree.

## Configure flags in the device tree

Build flags can also be set in the device's Bluenixx product makefile, typically named `bluenixx_<device>.mk`:

```make
RELEASE_TYPE := OFFICIAL
BLUENIXX_MAINTAINER := zedisspp
WITH_GMS := true
SURFACE_FLINGER_BOOST := true
```

Place these assignments **before the first `inherit-product` line**. The relevant `vendor/lineage` makefiles read the values when they are inherited, so assignments made afterward may not take effect.

Use `:=` to assign a value that overrides a value exported from the shell. Use `?=` if the value should act only as a default and remain overridable.

For an `OFFICIAL` build, ensure that the corresponding `maintainer:product` pair is present in `vendor/lineage/bluenixx.maintainers`.

## Signing builds

For release builds, configure signing keys and follow the Bluenixx signing template:

- [Bluenixx build signing template](https://github.com/Bluenixx/bluenixx-template-signing-builds)

Do not distribute a release build as officially signed unless the appropriate signing configuration has been applied.

---

Thank you for building Bluenixx.
